    "title": "Crews extinguish RV fire that spread to fireworks container, wooded area in NW Harris Co.: Officials - NewsBreak",
    "text": "3 hours ago\nFireworks were flying into the air, when a shipping container filled with them went up in flames in northwest Harris County, the fire marshal says.\nSpring FD officials said that fire crews responded to the fire just after 7 p.m. in the 23300 block of Kuykendahl.\nSpring FD officials said the fire started in an RV, spreading into an adjacent shipping container filled with fireworks, and then prompted a grass fire spreading into a wooded area and rail line.\nCrews from Spring FD, Klein FD, The Woodlands, Magnolia, and Tomball controlled the grass fire and extinguished the shipping container, fire officials said.\nAccording to officials, no injuries were reported.\nAn investigation is still ongoing.\nEyewitness News is gathering the facts on this breaking news story.",
    "summary": "Fireworks were flying into the air, when a shipping container filled with them went up in flames in northwest Harris County, the fire marshal says. Spring FD officials said that fire crews responded to the fire just after 7 p.m. in the 23300 block of Kuykendahl. Spring FD officials said the fire started in an RV, spreading into an adjacent shipping container filled with fireworks, and then prompted a grass fire spreading into a wooded area and rail line.",
